/*
 * Zephyr's rpi_5 takes zephyr,sram from the SoC's sram0
 * (dts/arm64/broadcom/bcm2712.dtsi: 512 KiB at 0x200000, two address cells).
 * This image carries the V3D's 48 MiB carve-out and the compiler's 2 MiB
 * scratch as statics, so it gets 96 MiB from 0x200000, as the Pi 4's gl_test
 * does (boards/rpi_4b.overlay). The firmware loads a kernel= image at
 * 0x200000 and puts the DTB at 0x2efec600 (driver/docs/rpi5-v3d71-facts.md,
 * U6), above the image's end at 0x6200000, and the range stays below 4 GiB,
 * so the V3D's page table entries and the mailbox's buffer address fit
 * (pre-study-rpi5.md, U10). The probes' 32 MiB from 0x200000
 * (tools/probes/rpi_5/rpi5_triangle/boards/rpi_5.overlay) are its front.
 * Zephyr's own mailbox driver (mbox0) stays disabled, as bcm2712.dtsi has it:
 * the board layer's rpi_mbox.c owns the mailbox.
 */
&sram0 {
	reg = <0x0 0x200000 0x6000000>;
};
